meta {
  name: Container recommendations - detail dual engine
  type: http
  seq: 67
}

get {
  url: {{baseURL}}/recommendations/openshift/{{recommendationUuid}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Container detail includes nested dual engines under each recommendation term.

  For test data where cost and performance sizing must differ, use the NISE fixture at
  `nise/examples/ocp_dual_engine/` (workloads: spike-cpu-api, steady-mem-worker).

  Inspect:
  recommendations.recommendation_terms.<term>.recommendation_engines.cost
  recommendations.recommendation_terms.<term>.recommendation_engines.performance

  Cost engine uses P60 CPU / P95 memory; performance engine uses P98 CPU / P100 memory.
  List endpoints accept filter[engine] to return only one engine block per term; detail
  always returns both when data exists.

  To observe divergent cost vs performance sizing, ingest data from nise/examples/ocp_dual_engine/.
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}
